{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 252,
    "dDurationMs": 2619,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- These are soft robots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2871,
    "dDurationMs": 2232,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their structural components are built,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5103,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not out of metal or wood,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7223,
    "dDurationMs": 3884,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but flexible materials\nlike plastic tubing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11107,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how do they work?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12907,
    "dDurationMs": 4383,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and why would you want a soft\nrobot in the first place?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17290,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video was sponsored by KiwiCo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19430,
    "dDurationMs": 3096,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Check out their robots\nat the end of the show."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22526,
    "dDurationMs": 2924,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(machine blowing)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25450,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I came up to Stanford"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27110,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to meet Zach Hammond and his soft robot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30310,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How's it going?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31740,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All right, you want to tip it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36700,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So is the idea that the\nrobot could walk this way?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40680,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Totally, yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41513,
    "dDurationMs": 2947,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can kind of chain\nthese rolls together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44460,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to kind of roll around in any environment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47310,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They call this punctuated\nrolling locomotion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49740,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wherein it's kind of stuck"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51450,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a face until it tips over and now it's\non a new face and it can then continue to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55660,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "move its center of gravity. Once that center\nof gravity exits the support polygon or the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60690,
    "dDurationMs": 5570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "base, then it tips over one of the edges of\nthe face."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66260,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is a different soft robot made out\nof flexible tubing. It was designed to mimic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71920,
    "dDurationMs": 6750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the way a turtle walks, where diagonally opposite\nlegs move together. It's powered entirely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78670,
    "dDurationMs": 7570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by compressed air and perhaps most impressive,\nit requires no electronics. All of the circuitry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86240,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is pneumatic and this means the robot can\nbe used in places like mines, where electronics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92160,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could spark explosions, or in the strong magnetic\nfields around MRI machines. But why would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99280,
    "dDurationMs": 2699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you want a soft robot in the first place?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101979,
    "dDurationMs": 3721,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- One of the things that I like to do is just\nto take the robot and kind of like beat it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105700,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up a little bit and show how it's compliant\nand compressive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109590,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Nope, because they're safer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110940,
    "dDurationMs": 2590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If you'd like to take a whack at it, you\nknow, feel free."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113530,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But I don't think this is your work, I don't\nwant to break it, obviously."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116310,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- No, feel free, go for it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117310,
    "dDurationMs": 6970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- For operation around humans, there's not\nmuch damage a soft robot can do to you. I"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124280,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can stand on these?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126000,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yep."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127000,
    "dDurationMs": 3119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is a pretty crazy compliant robot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130119,
    "dDurationMs": 5631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Because the the fundamental structure of\nthis robot is compliant, there's only some"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135750,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maximum force that it could ever exert on\nme. So it's inherently safe to be operating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140640,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around people."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142340,
    "dDurationMs": 5569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Could we make it fall and have me be inside\nit?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147909,
    "dDurationMs": 3261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah. Yeah, we could do that for sure. Just\nwatch your head."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151170,
    "dDurationMs": 1281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yep, if I go over here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152451,
    "dDurationMs": 1678,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If you're there, yeah, we can do that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154129,
    "dDurationMs": 9011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- All right, let's try it. Here it comes.\nWell, that's not bad at all. Is it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163140,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I can try another shape. That's supposed\nto open up one of the faces, so you can jump"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167660,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of it quickly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168660,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169660,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I haven't tested it in a little while, so..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170660,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Sure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171660,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I don't know how it's gonna go, but let's\ntry this. There you go that's the face right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174760,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there to your right and you can exit the trust\nfrom that face."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178330,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Boom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179330,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Perfect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180330,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Just that easy. Did you build this by yourself?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183640,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Me and one other grad student built this\nentire thing ourselves, basically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187930,
    "dDurationMs": 1060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And how long did it take?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188990,
    "dDurationMs": 4169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We did it in about a month, I want to say,\nlike actually constructing everything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193159,
    "dDurationMs": 2271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And was it tricky? I mean, were you sewing\nthat stuff?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195430,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yep, we sewed this all ourselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197310,
    "dDurationMs": 5310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The main structural members of this robot\nare fabric tubes inflated with air."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202620,
    "dDurationMs": 6759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, so these red tubes are a nylon fabric\nand then internally, there is a polyethylene"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209379,
    "dDurationMs": 2950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tube that provides the air tightness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212329,
    "dDurationMs": 5631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The tubes are inflated to about six PSI\nabove atmospheric. So it's almost one and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217960,
    "dDurationMs": 6109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a half atmospheres. Each tube passes through\npairs of rollers connected to a motor. The"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224069,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rollers pinch the tube, so it bends kind of\nlike a pinched straw."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227889,
    "dDurationMs": 3861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Add the rods and then we have this like\nhigh friction material wrapped around the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231750,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rods. And then that coupled with the fact\nthat we have this pressurized tube that's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235580,
    "dDurationMs": 4329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kind of pushing the membrane of the tube into\nthe rollers, prevents us from slipping."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239909,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- By driving the motor, it changes the length\nof the tubes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243879,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Kind of like when a clown creates a twist\nin a balloon and then folds that balloon into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249519,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a balloon animal. The difference between what\nthe clown does and what we do is that there's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254069,
    "dDurationMs": 5341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some passage of air between adjacent segments\nof the tube. So that as the robot drives around,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259410,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're not pressurizing the segments of the\ntube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262350,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This robot is made of four inflated tubes,\neach one connected to a pair of motors, forming"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267490,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "triangular sides."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269130,
    "dDurationMs": 3711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We also think that they kind of look like\nsausage links when put together, which is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272841,
    "dDurationMs": 5269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why we've named these robots after different\nsausages. So this one's called Polish, that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278110,
    "dDurationMs": 4990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one over there is Chorizo, There's a Linguica\nand a kielbasa over there somewhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283100,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So what shape is the overall thing? It's\nan octahedron?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285460,
    "dDurationMs": 5730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, we call it an octahedron because if\nyou drew lines between these kind of kinematic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291190,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "joints here, it would create an octahedral\nshape."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294990,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Driving the motors together, allows the\nrobot to dramatically change shape. It can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299020,
    "dDurationMs": 7560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get very tall or short and squat. But since\nthe tubes themselves don't change in length,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306580,
    "dDurationMs": 5230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the overall perimeter of the robot, the length\nof all the edges combined doesn't change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311810,
    "dDurationMs": 7240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the robot is considered isoparametric.\nHow do you feel when you watch those Boston"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319050,
    "dDurationMs": 1009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dynamics videos?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320059,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh, I love those videos, they're so cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322139,
    "dDurationMs": 1791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The Boston Dynamics robots are kind of terrifying."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323930,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Mm-hmm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324930,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I guess and the idea with soft robots, it's\nto like convince people that robots are good"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328130,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and soft and kind, and friendly and fake?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330620,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's definitely true, yeah. There are\nsome things that you can do to rigid systems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334650,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make them feel like compliant systems based\non how you're controlling the motors. But"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339050,
    "dDurationMs": 5110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yeah, they're definitely, you know, heavy\nexpensive and can be dangerous if they're"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344160,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not used correctly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345890,
    "dDurationMs": 5830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The hard robots we're used to are strong\nand precise. Their actions are accurate and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351720,
    "dDurationMs": 5950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "repeatable, but they are also heavy and they\ncan't really change their volume as dramatically,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357670,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this robot is still capable of carrying\na heavy load."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362380,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So I have a GUI in MATLAB."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364080,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh nice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365080,
    "dDurationMs": 4619,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That enables me to just put in the positions\nthat I want the robots to move in inches and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369699,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then send them out. There's another other\nfunctionality of some like stored configurations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374009,
    "dDurationMs": 1451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to send to the robots."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375460,
    "dDurationMs": 5250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Soft robots also have the advantage of shape\nchanging. They can become tall to go over"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380710,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "obstacles or short to fit under obstructions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384350,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So if there is some rock that it didn't\nsee or that it wanted to roll over. It could"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388970,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simply do that and the compliance of the tubes\nwould simply just bend around that disturbance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394850,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Do you imagine robots like this doing work\nin space?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398460,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh yeah, definitely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399750,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So one of the nice things about these types\nof structures is that they can shrink down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404020,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their volume very drastically. And because\nvolume on rockets is such an expensive premium,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410740,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being able to have a robot that can pack down\nsmall for transport is very valuable. So NASA"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415400,
    "dDurationMs": 5139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was at one point looking into trust robots\nfor exactly that reason. And they've contacted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420539,
    "dDurationMs": 5651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "us since we've made this robot to explore\ndifferent ideas for space exploration projects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426190,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So one of the things that they're thinking\nabout doing is deploying robots underneath"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429620,
    "dDurationMs": 5150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a sheet of ice. So they're gonna drill through\nthis sheet of ice and then deposit a robot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434770,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through what is a kind of a small diameter\nhole. And so if you can have a robot that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439350,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can change its volume very drastically or\nbe disassembled and then reassembled to form"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444910,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like a much larger structure. Then you can\nhave large robots that are able to fit through"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449910,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these tight spaces and be deployed in kind\nof difficult to access areas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453670,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Is this a little bit like an octopus? Is\nthat how you could think of it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458000,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There is some connection there because they\nuse their shape changing ability and their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461630,
    "dDurationMs": 6039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compliance to squeeze through tight passageways,\nand then also to wrap their body around objects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467669,
    "dDurationMs": 3631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So for example, they can open jars with their\ntentacles, and one of the things that we want"
    } ]
  }, {
